    "body": "AFAICT, an underscore in the domain part currently results in `.validity` reporting `typeMismatch: true` in Firefox, Safari, and Chrome. As far as I'm aware, this isn't a source of complaints, so it seems OK to keep using the STD3 ASCII deny list.",
